This is the source listingh for ST Comm, a communications program I wrote.
It allows 'unlimited' save capability to either disk or printer.  It does not
include XMODEM capability.  If some knowledgable soul will send me an 
explanation of the protocol, I will include it in the program and repost the
source.  This program was created with the Hippo C compiler.  It runs on
an Atari 520ST under HOS or as a stand alone, dependent upon compiler options at
compile time.
This is not a final version, however, it does work.
When performing any kind of text save, the save buffers are flushed every-
time that the save option is toggled off.  If you are finished saving to
a disk file, be sure to close the file before saving to a different file.
For instance, if you are saving to a disk file, when you toggle the disk save
option off, the save buffer is written to the file, then cleared.  Performing
a close command from the main menu also flushes any save buffers.
Also, when transitioning from terminal mode to offline, if you are
saving text, the buffers will be flushed before the Main Menu is displayed.
